// HumanityOS home design: the HOMESTEAD FOR A HOUSEHOLD (34 x 55 m plot, up to five people in four
// bedrooms). Approved by the operator 2026-11-13 (docs/design/home-room-program.md, section 5 and
// "His answers"): every room earns its walls with a function its neighbours cannot share, and every
// size comes from the room program (section 2), not from a ladder of squares. Only the plot is
// Fibonacci (mothership master plan 1.5). A start of its own (data/homes/starts.ron); today's
// homestead (data/homes/homestead.ron) stays the default until the wipe decides.
//
// FRAME. Home-local metres from the box's min corner, x east, z south, like every home design. The
// street is WEST (x < 0): plots of this kind stand on the east side of First Street
// (data/blueprints/ship_structure.ron), and the door is in the west wall. Drawn with the street at
// the top, the plan reads as the approved draft: data x is the distance from the street and data z
// is 34 less the distance along the street (a quarter turn, not a mirror). `node
// scripts/draw-homes.js <folder>` draws every floor from this file, street up, with the room
// table, so the drawings and the game cannot disagree.
//
// THE PLAN, street first: the front garden and drive (x 0..3); the HOUSE (x 3..13, z 23..34) with
// the YARD (z 12..23) and the WORKSHOP AND VEHICLE BAY (z 0..12, its folding door on the drive)
// beside it; the back terrace (x 13..16); the GREENHOUSE (x 16..36, 616 m2 of growing floor) with
// the harvest store and the mushroom room at its house end and the side path along it (z 0..2);
// then the ORCHARD and its beds, the hen range for ten with its hen house (31 m from the house),
// the rabbits, the compost bays and the hives (x 36..55).
//
// THE HOUSE. Ground floor: living room 4.5 x 5 m, kitchen and dining 5.5 x 5 m (a wide sliding
// door between them), entry 2 x 2 m, hall and stair 8 x 2 m, utility (mudroom, laundry, the ship's
// life-support hookups) 3 x 4 m, shower room 2 x 4 m, main bedroom 4 x 4 m and its walk-in
// wardrobe 1 x 4 m, so the whole home works step-free. Upper floor (slab top 3.0) over the quiet
// wing only: bathroom 2.5 x 4 m and bedrooms 2, 3 and 4, each 2.5 x 4 m (10 m2, over England's
// 7.5 m2 single and 2.15 m width), and the upper hall with the landing and the linen cupboard
// round the stairwell, guarded by 1.0 m steel balustrades. The bathroom sits over the shower room
// and utility, so the water runs in one stack; the living room and kitchen stay one storey.
//
// THE STAIR: "stairs_house" (data/blueprints/structure_types.ron), the stairs finding's numbers
// (docs/reference/findings/2026-10-20-stairs-guards-and-headroom.md): 16 risers of 187.5 mm on
// 254 mm goings, 1.0 m wide, climbing east (+x) along the hall to the landing at x 10.
//
// WALLS. House rooms 3.0 m oak inside, 3.0 m concrete outside; the workshop, stores and the
// outside of the house concrete; the greenhouse glass; the animal houses timber; the garden's own
// boundaries 2.0 m pine fences with gates (2.0 m so each part of the garden is a room of its own:
// a lower fence lets the room finder join it to its neighbours, and a 2 m screen also sends the
// bees' flight path up over head height). Lids at 3.0: solid over the house rooms, the stores and
// the animal houses (dark bedrooms: at most 1 lux to sleep, docs/reference/findings/
// 2026-11-06-noise-and-sleep.md), glass over the workshop; the greenhouse and the garden rise to
// the 6 m glass roof.
//
// WHAT THIS SHAPE CANNOT HOLD YET (each listed in docs/design/home-room-program.md section 8 with
// the rung that adds it): windows and a second gate in the plot's shell (the vehicle gate on the
// street, the living room's side windows); animals, the honeybee hives and the orchard's trees and
// beds as things (the zones say where they go); the fan lines (machines in
// data/machines/household_homestead.ron).
//
// Materials: 0 = grid, 1 = steel/metal, 2 = concrete, 3 = wood, 4 = glass, 6 = pine,
// 9 = steel balustrade.

